@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- UIC (Công ty Bảo hiểm Liên hiệp) Property All Risks wording, "QUY TẮC BẢO HIỂM MỌI RỦI RO TÀI SẢN".
-- THE NOUNS: DECLARE and nothing else. Every other module imports this one.
--
-- Source: ../../source/raw/uic-par.txt, the `pdftotext -layout` rendering of
-- https://uic.vn/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/UIC-PAR-Quy-tac-bao-hiem.pdf (8 pages, PDF sha256
-- 02379990...ee7a), retrieved 2026-10-06. A `src:N` comment quotes line N of that file and is
-- generated by tools/vnsrc.py; no Vietnamese here is typed by hand.
--
-- Money is Vietnamese dong (VND) as a bare NUMBER. Days are calendar days and months calendar
-- months unless a rule says otherwise (NOTES.md, forks F29 and F26).
--
-- Membership test for this module: a witness of ordinary competence (the insured, an adjuster,
-- a schedule, a receipt) could testify to the fact. Whether the fact makes the loss covered or
-- changes the amount is a rule, and lives in the module for the provision that says so.
--
-- The document defines almost nothing itself. It leaves to the Schedule, src:11:
--   "Bản tóm tắt Hợp đồng bảo hiểm"
-- the Period of Insurance, the items and their sums insured, the limit of liability, the
-- deductible and the premises. Every one of those is an input here, with no default.

§ `Nouns for the UIC Property All Risks wording`

§§ `The parties`

-- The insurer, defined in the opening words, and the insured, never defined (a term of the
-- Schedule; General Condition 1, src:276-279, carries Schedule definitions into the wording).
-- src:3 | Công ty Bảo hiểm Liên hiệp (sau đây gọi tắt là Công ty Bảo hiểm) đồng ý rằng (trên cơ sở các điều
DECLARE `A party` IS ONE OF
    `the Insurer`
    `the Insured`

§§ `The Schedule, and the Policy as it stands`

-- One item of the Schedule, with its sum insured (insuring clause, proviso (i), src:25-26).
DECLARE `An item in the Schedule` HAS
    `the description of the item` IS A STRING
    `the sum insured for the item` IS A NUMBER

-- A later period for which the Insured paid a premium that the Insurer accepted, renewing the
-- Policy (insuring clause, src:11-13).
DECLARE `A renewal` HAS
    `the first day of the renewal period`   IS A DATE
    `the last day of the renewal period`    IS A DATE
    `the Insured paid the premium for it`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Insurer accepted that payment`     IS A BOOLEAN

-- General Condition 3 (src:292-298): ended at the Insured's written request, or by the
-- Insurer on 30 days' notice. The Insured's request is taken to say from when it takes
-- effect (fork F28); the Insurer's notice takes effect 30 days after it is sent (fork F27).
DECLARE `A termination of the Policy` IS ONE OF
    `not terminated`
    `terminated at the Insured's written request, with effect from`
        HAS `the date it takes effect` IS A DATE
    `terminated by the Insurer, by written notice sent on`
        HAS `the date the notice was sent` IS A DATE

-- What the Schedule and the payment record say. `the limit of liability` and `the deductible
-- for each loss` are MAYBE: the Schedule may state none, and the wording says what follows
-- (no limit beyond the sums insured; nothing deducted).
DECLARE `The Policy` HAS
    `the first day of the Period of Insurance` IS A DATE
    `the last day of the Period of Insurance`  IS A DATE
    `the date the first premium was paid`      IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the renewals`                             IS A LIST OF `A renewal`
    `the items`                                IS A LIST OF `An item in the Schedule`
    `the limit of liability`                   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the deductible for each loss`             IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the premium for the Period of Insurance`  IS A NUMBER
    `the termination`                          IS A `A termination of the Policy`

§§ `Causes`

-- Every cause the wording names, in the order it names them, and one catch-all. A cause the
-- wording does not name is covered unless something else excludes it: this is an all-risks
-- form ("do những nguyên nhân không bị loại trừ", src:9).
--
-- Each constructor renders the Vietnamese limb it is listed under; GLOSSARY.md gives the
-- verbatim words and the translation risk of each.
DECLARE `A cause` IS ONE OF
    -- Exclusion A1(a)(i), src:43-45
    `faulty or defective design or materials`
    `faulty or defective workmanship`
    `inherent vice`
    `latent defect`
    `gradual deterioration`
    `deformation or distortion`
    `wear and tear`
    -- Exclusion A1(a)(ii), src:47-49
    `interruption of the water, gas, electricity or fuel supply`
    `failure of a system carrying waste into or out of the Insured Premises`
    -- Exclusion A1(b)(i), src:55
    `collapse or cracking of buildings`
    -- Exclusion A1(b)(ii), src:57-60
    `corrosion or rust`
    `extremes or changes of temperature, humidity or dryness`
    `wet or dry rot`
    `fungus or mould`
    `shrinkage, evaporation or loss of weight`
    `change in colour, flavour, texture or finish`
    `action of light`
    `vermin or insects`
    `scratching or marring`
    -- Exclusion A1(c), src:69-85
    `theft`
    `fraudulent or dishonest acts`
    `disappearance, unexplained shortage, or shortage found at stocktaking`
    `misfiling or misplacement of information`
    `shortage in the supply or distribution of materials`
    `shortage due to an error in accounting or record-keeping`
    `cracking, fracture, collapse or overheating of boilers, economisers, vessels or pipes containing liquid or gas`
    `leakage at joints or failure of welds of boilers`
    `mechanical or electrical breakdown or derangement of machinery or equipment`
    `bursting, overflowing, discharge or leakage of water from tanks, apparatus or pipes`
    -- Exclusion A1(d), src:97-107
    `river or sea erosion`
    `subsidence, ground movement or landslip`
    `normal settlement of new structures`
    `wind`
    `rain`
    `hail`
    `frost`
    `snow`
    `flood`
    `sand or dust`
    `freezing or solidification of molten material`
    `accidental discharge of molten material`
    -- Exclusion A2, src:111-115
    `a wilful act or wilful negligence of the Insured or of anyone acting on their behalf`
    `cessation of work`
    `delay`
    `loss of market`
    `another consequential or indirect loss`
    -- Exclusion A3(a), src:120-121
    `war`
    `invasion`
    `act of a foreign enemy`
    `hostilities or warlike operations, whether war be declared or not`
    `civil war`
    -- Exclusion A3(b), src:123-124. `riot or rebellion` renders the one word the wording
    -- uses both here and in the carve-back to Exclusion B1 (fork F7, finding 1).
    `uprising`
    `civil commotion assuming the proportions of, or leading to, a popular rising`
    `mutiny or military rising`
    `insurrection`
    `riot or rebellion`
    `revolution`
    `military action or usurped power`
    -- Exclusion A3(c), src:130-145
    `an act of terrorism`
    `action taken in controlling, preventing or suppressing an act of terrorism`
    -- Exclusion A3(d)-(e), src:155-166
    `confiscation, nationalisation, requisition for military purposes or expropriation by a lawfully constituted authority`
    `unlawful occupation of a building by any person`
    `destruction by order of a public authority`
    -- Exclusion A4, src:176-180
    `nuclear weapons material`
    `ionising radiation or radioactive contamination from nuclear fuel or nuclear waste`
    -- The perils of the carve-back to Exclusion B1 not named above, src:202-207
    `fire`
    `lightning`
    `explosion`
    `falling aircraft`
    `strike`
    `locked-out workers`
    `persons taking part in labour disturbances`
    `malicious persons`
    `impact by a road vehicle`
    `impact by an animal`
    `earthquake`
    `storm`
    -- Exclusions B3(f)-(h), src:229-238, and B5, src:247-249
    `a process the property was undergoing`
    `installation, moving or relocation of machinery or equipment, including dismantling and re-erection`
    `work on the property: refurbishing, repair, testing, installation or servicing`
    `explosion or rupture of a boiler, economiser, turbine, or other vessel, machinery or apparatus in which pressure is used`
    -- Anything else: "accidental breakage" by a dropped tool, say.
    `a cause this wording does not name`

§§ `Kinds of property`

-- The kinds of property Exclusion B names (src:187-249), and two that other provisions need:
-- buildings (Exclusion A1(b)(i), General Condition 8) and machinery or equipment (B3(g)).
-- A piece of property may be of several kinds at once (a computer held in trust is both
-- B1(d) and B2), so a piece carries a LIST of these.
DECLARE `A kind of property` IS ONE OF
    -- Exclusion B1(a), src:187-190
    `money, cheques, stamps, bonds, credit cards or securities of any description`
    `jewellery, precious stones, precious metals, gold or silver`
    `furs`
    `curiosities, rare books or works of art`
    -- Exclusion B1(b)-(d), src:195-200
    `fixed glass`
    `glassware other than fixed glass, china, earthenware, marble, or another fragile or brittle article`
    `electronic systems, computers or data processing equipment`
    -- Exclusion B2, src:209-211
    `goods held on consignment or in trust`
    `documents, manuscripts or business books`
    `data stored in computer systems`
    `patterns, models, moulds, plans or designs`
    `explosives`
    -- Exclusion B3(a), src:213-215 (fork F10 on the word rendered "rolling stock")
    `a road-licensed vehicle, caravan, trailer, locomotive, rolling stock, watercraft, aircraft, spacecraft or the like`
    -- Exclusion B3(d), src:223-226
    `land, driveways, pavements, roads, runways, railway lines, dams, reservoirs, canals, rigs, wells, pipelines, tunnels, bridges, docks, piers, jetties, excavations, wharves, mines, or underground or offshore works`
    -- Exclusion B3(e), src:227
    `livestock, crops or trees`
    -- Exclusion A1(d)(iv), src:103-105
    `fences or gates`
    -- Exclusion B5, src:247-249
    `a boiler, economiser, turbine, or other vessel, machinery or apparatus in which pressure is used, or its contents`
    -- Named by no exclusion, but needed by one
    `a building`
    `machinery or equipment`
    `property of any other kind`

§§ `The circumstances of the property at the time of the Loss`

-- Facts about where or how the property was when it was lost or damaged, each the hinge of
-- one provision.
DECLARE `A circumstance of the property` IS ONE OF
    -- Exclusion A1(c)(i), src:69-70: the theft was at a building entered or left by force
    `stolen at a building with force and violence used to enter it or to escape from it`
    -- Exclusion A1(c)(vi), src:84-85
    `in a building that was empty or not in use`
    -- Exclusion A1(d)(iv), src:103-105
    `movable property in the open, or in a building not enclosed on all sides`
    -- Exclusion A3(d), proviso, src:161-164
    `lost or damaged before a dispossession, or during one that was temporary`
    -- Exclusion B3(b), src:217-218
    `in transit outside the Insured Premises named in the Schedule`
    -- Exclusion B3(c), src:220-221
    `in the course of demolition, construction or erection, or materials or supplies for that work`
    -- Exclusion B3(i), src:240
    `insured separately under another, separate policy`

§§ `What happened to the property, and what it is worth`

-- The insuring clause pays "the value of the property at the time of its loss or
-- destruction, or the amount of the damage" (src:15-17). Which of the two is a fact about
-- the property; the figure is an assessed input.
DECLARE `What happened to the property` IS ONE OF
    `lost or destroyed, its value at the time of the Loss being`
        HAS `the value at the time of the Loss` IS A NUMBER
    `damaged, the amount of the damage being`
        HAS `the amount of the damage` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Alterations under General Condition 8`

-- The four events of General Condition 8 (src:360-376) after which cover on the affected
-- property ceases unless the Insurer consented by endorsement before the loss.
DECLARE `A change under General Condition 8` IS ONE OF
    -- (a), first limb (fork F21: no "increase of risk" qualifier on this limb)
    `the trade or manufacture carried on was altered`
    -- (a), second limb
    `the use of the building, or other circumstances affecting it, changed so as to increase the risk`
    -- (b): the number of days the building had been unoccupied when the loss happened
    `the building had been unoccupied, for this many days, when the loss happened`
        HAS `the number of days` IS A NUMBER
    -- (c)
    `the property was removed to a building or place other than the Insured Premises`
    -- (d)
    `the Insured's interest in the property passed to another`
        HAS `by will or by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `An alteration under General Condition 8` HAS
    `what changed`                                                     IS A `A change under General Condition 8`
    `the Insurer's consent was endorsed on the Policy before the loss` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Other insurance of the property`

-- Exclusion B4 (src:242-245) and General Condition 6 (src:331-336) turn on other insurance.
-- B4 measures this Policy's share by what the other policies would have paid had this one
-- not been in force; that figure is a fact about the other policies' terms.
DECLARE `Other insurance of the property` IS ONE OF
    `no other insurance`
    `insured by other policies in force at the time of the Loss`
        HAS `what those policies would have paid had this Policy not been in force` IS A NUMBER
    `not insured elsewhere, but it would have been, were it not for this Policy`
        HAS `what those policies would have paid` IS A NUMBER

§§ `The Loss`

-- One piece of property lost or damaged in the Loss, with the causal chain that reached it.
--
-- THE CHAIN. `the direct cause` is the cause that acted on this property; `the earlier causes
-- in the chain` are the causes that led to it, in sequence (wear and tear, then the fire it
-- started); `the other contributing causes` acted at the same time, outside that sequence.
-- `the earlier Loss it directly resulted from, by cause` is the cause of an earlier Loss to
-- Insured Property, or to premises containing it, of which this damage was the direct result
-- (rust after a fire): the hinge of the exceptions to Exclusions A1(b) and A1(c),
-- src:65-67 and 93-95. NOTHING where there was none.
DECLARE `A piece of property lost or damaged` HAS
    `what it is`                                              IS A LIST OF `A kind of property`
    `specially stated in the Policy as insured`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `its circumstances`                                       IS A LIST OF `A circumstance of the property`
    `the direct cause`                                        IS A `A cause`
    `the earlier causes in the chain`                         IS A LIST OF `A cause`
    `the other contributing causes`                           IS A LIST OF `A cause`
    `the earlier Loss it directly resulted from, by cause`    IS A MAYBE `A cause`
    `what happened to it`                                     IS A `What happened to the property`
    `affected by a misdescription, misrepresentation or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the alterations before the loss`                         IS A LIST OF `An alteration under General Condition 8`

-- The property under one item of the Schedule that the Loss reached. The value of ALL the
-- property under the item (not only what was lost) is what the Under-insurance condition
-- compares with the item's sum insured (src:253-257).
DECLARE `A loss under an item` HAS
    `the item`                                                            IS AN `An item in the Schedule`
    `the value of all the property under the item at the time of the Loss` IS A NUMBER
    `the amount already paid under the item for earlier losses in the period` IS A NUMBER
    `other insurance of the property`                                     IS AN `Other insurance of the property`
    `the property lost or damaged`                                        IS A LIST OF `A piece of property lost or damaged`

-- One occurrence ("mỗi vụ tổn thất", src:22). The four adjectives are the insuring clause's
-- and the defined term's (src:9, 16-19); each is a finding of fact about the occurrence.
-- `the amount already paid for earlier losses in the period` is the total paid under every
-- item, for the limit of liability and the total sum insured (src:22-28).
DECLARE `The Loss` HAS
    `the date of the Loss`      IS A DATE
    `physical`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `accidental`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `sudden`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `unforeseen`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the losses under each item` IS A LIST OF `A loss under an item`
    `the amount already paid for earlier losses in the period` IS A NUMBER

§§ `The claim`

-- What the Insured and the Insurer did after the Loss: General Conditions 4, 5, 9, 10 and 13,
-- the deductible undertaking (src:267-269) and General Condition 12. Dates are calendar dates;
-- a MAYBE DATE is NOTHING where the step was not taken.
DECLARE `The claim` HAS
    -- General Condition 9, src:380-414
    `the date the Insured became aware of the event`                        IS A DATE
    `the Insured took steps at once to minimise the loss and recover lost property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Insured notified the Insurer in writing at once`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `theft, suspected theft, or a wilful or malicious act was involved`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Insured notified the police at once`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the written claim and particulars of other insurances were delivered` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date to which the Insurer extended the time in writing`            IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the Insured produced the further particulars and the declaration of truth` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- General Condition 4(a), src:304-307: ANY claim under the Policy ("bất kỳ khiếu nại nào"),
    -- not only this one
    `a claim under the Policy was fraudulent, a false declaration supported one, or fraudulent means were used` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- General Conditions 4(b) and 12, src:309-312, 481-483
    `the date the claim was rejected`                                       IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date an action was commenced`                                      IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date the dispute was referred to arbitration`                      IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date of the arbitration award`                                     IS A MAYBE DATE
    -- General Condition 10, src:442-445
    `the Insured, or anyone for them, failed to comply with the Insurer's requirements under General Condition 10, or obstructed it` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- General Condition 5, src:316-327
    `the Insured failed to do or permit the acts the Insurer reasonably required to enforce its rights against others` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- General Condition 13, src:487-488
    `the Insured failed to maintain the property or to take reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- The deductible undertaking, src:267-269
    `the Insured insured the deductible elsewhere`                          IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Acts, for the duties`

-- The acts the regulative rules (General Conditions 3, 5, 7, 9, 10, 11 and 13 and the
-- deductible undertaking) speak of.
DECLARE `An act` IS ONE OF
    `take steps to minimise the loss and recover lost property`
    `notify the Insurer in writing`
    `notify the police`
    `deliver the written claim and particulars of other insurances`
    `produce the further particulars, documents and declaration of truth`
    `do and permit the acts the Insurer reasonably requires to enforce its rights against others`
    `demand the refund of premium`
    `refund premium in proportion to the unexpired period`
    `insure the deductible`
    `appoint an arbitrator`
    `appoint a sole arbitrator`
    `furnish plans, specifications, measurements, quantities and particulars for reinstatement`
    `maintain the property and take all reasonable precautions to prevent Loss`
    `obstruct the Insurer in exercising its powers under General Condition 10`

§§ `Who bears the burden of proof`

-- Exclusion A3 (src:147-150, 168-171) puts the burden of proving cover on the Insured.
DECLARE `A bearer of the burden of proof` IS ONE OF
    `the Insured bears it`
